      "value": "@{5bafbca9282d5d55fb6899f8|full_name}: It is a solution. It's one of 2 solutions actually. That's why the implimented the safety system in the first place, the only other thing you can do is learn the name of the shader, let the devs know and they can try to black list it. Sure the shades can be abused and be annoying but there are just as many people that do cool creative stuff with them as there are people who just want to be crazy. Use the safety system, that's what it's there for.",
